| `tests/integration/test_config_reads_gate.py` | Fails a direct read of `config/project.json` or `config/practices.json`, or of a variable the config declares, outside `scripts/config_loader.py`, so a default, a type and a secret are judged by one rule; each finding is one line naming the file, the line, the rule and the fix. | `make test` | [`config_reads.roots`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`config_reads.allowed.<name>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`expiring_tier.expires`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | A heuristic over the syntax tree: it cannot see a path handed in as a parameter, a function of another module that opens what it is given, a method called through an object, a variable name held in a variable, or a read through `subprocess` or `importlib`. In a generated project its two finding tests judge through `scripts/expiring_tier.py`: a finding `expiring_tier.baseline` records warns until `expiring_tier.expires`, and any other is red. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
